    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 11484,
        "name": "Zembar",
        "username": "Zembar",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/z/779978/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-03T04:06:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Do hazard attacks trigger when they are used?  Like the ice spike attack from Absolute Zero.  When it’s played does it hit anything that goes under it?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Do drones suffer an attack if they’re on a hazard but didn’t activate?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>If Omnitron is on a hazard (either placed under him or moved last turn)  And he decides to move “through” it, causing another hex of his to move into the hazard, does it trigger?</p>\n</li>\n</ol>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:48.099Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 5,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 25.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 11483,
        "topic_slug": "hazard-attacks",
        "display_username": "Zembar",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "1. Do hazard attacks trigger when they are used?  Like the ice spike attack from Absolute Zero.  When it's played does it hit anything that goes under it?\r\n\r\n2.  Do drones suffer an attack if they're on a hazard but didn't activate?\r\n\r\n3.  If Omnitron is on a hazard (either placed under him or moved last turn)  And he decides to move \"through\" it, causing another hex of his to move into the hazard, does it trigger?",
        "actions_summary": [],
        "moderator": false,
        "admin": false,
        "staff": false,
        "user_id": 579,
        "hidden": false,
        "trust_level": 1,
        "deleted_at": null,
        "user_deleted": false,
        "edit_reason": null,
        "can_view_edit_history": true,
        "wiki": false,
        "can_accept_answer": false,
        "can_unaccept_answer": false,
        "accepted_answer": false,
        "topic_accepted_answer": false
      },
      {
        "id": 120010,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-03T13:10:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>1. No, only when a target moves into it or when the target ends their turn on a Hazard space.</p><p>2. I think they do.</p><p>3. No, because he was already on the space before, so it's not a target moving through the space.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:53:22.300Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 11483,
        "topic_slug": "hazard-attacks",
        "display_username": "Ronway",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>1. No, only when a target moves into it or when the target ends their turn on a Hazard space.</p><p>2. I think they do.</p><p>3. No, because he was already on the space before, so it&#39;s not a target moving through the space.</p>",
        "actions_summary": [],
        "moderator": false,
        "admin": false,
        "staff": false,
        "user_id": 10,
        "hidden": false,
        "trust_level": 2,
        "deleted_at": null,
        "user_deleted": false,
        "edit_reason": null,
        "can_view_edit_history": true,
