      {
        "id": 120011,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-03T13:40:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>2. &nbsp;Yes they would, at the end of the Villain turn, all targets brought into play by powers of the villain, that do not get their own turn also trigger hazards.</p><p>3. &nbsp;When Omniron moves it is not three hexes moving, you select one Hex omnitron occupied and move with that hex, then set him back down on the final Hex. &nbsp;So when moving Omnitron has a profile of one hex, so you aren't continuing through it unless you choose to, and Omnitron could move through a one hex opening between two hazard spaces wihtout triggering them, but he will trigger things for setting his other two hexes when you set him back down.</p><p>That said, he is one target, and multiple hexes of Omnitron will not trigger the same hazard</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:53:22.371Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
