        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>2. &nbsp;Yes they would, at the end of the Villain turn, all targets brought into play by powers of the villain, that do not get their own turn also trigger hazards.</p><p>3. &nbsp;When Omniron moves it is not three hexes moving, you select one Hex omnitron occupied and move with that hex, then set him back down on the final Hex. &nbsp;So when moving Omnitron has a profile of one hex, so you aren&#39;t continuing through it unless you choose to, and Omnitron could move through a one hex opening between two hazard spaces wihtout triggering them, but he will trigger things for setting his other two hexes when you set him back down.</p><p>That said, he is one target, and multiple hexes of Omnitron will not trigger the same hazard</p>",
